<title>UK: Nigeria tells OPEC it produced at quota in February.</title>
<headline>Nigeria tells OPEC it produced at quota in February.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria said it pumped 1.865 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude in February, in line with its output quota, the OPEC news agency reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The data was provided in a monthly submission to OPEC headquarters in Vienna.</p>
<p>Nigeria said supply to market was also 1.865 million bpd. A survey by Reuters for February output showed Nigeria to be up at 2.15 million bpd, or 285,000 bpd above its quota.</p>
<p>All 11 OPEC members have now submitted supply and output data for February.</p>
<p>Supply as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for February is as follows:</p>
<p>    Algeria   0.797  0.783</p>
<p>    Indonesia 1.3253 1.3286</p>
<p>    Iran	3.5910 3.5910</p>
<p>    Iraq	1.2900 1.2900</p>
<p>    Kuwait    2.0082 2.0075</p>
<p>    Libya     1.3920 1.3970</p>
<p>    Nigeria   1.865  1.865</p>
<p>    Qatar     0.4022 0.3866</p>
<p>    Saudi     8.0083 8.0070</p>
<p>    UAE	 2.2523 2.1605</p>
<p>    Venezuela 2.4000 2.3951</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7629</p>
</text>
